<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16424" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-văcŭo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a., <i>to empty out</i>, <i>evacuate</i>
			(post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alvum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					20, 6, 23, § 52</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">32, 9, 33,
				§ 104</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>To rid one's self of</i>, <i>lay
			aside</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae pueruli erant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					1 Cor. 13, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>To make void</i>, <i>cancel</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obligationem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 8, 43, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Cor. 1, 17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
